00:19:00,480 --> 00:19:01,890
Why is he alone?

270
00:19:04,380 --> 00:19:07,020
One blast for a ranger returning;

271
00:19:07,030 --> 00:19:08,790
two for wildlings;

272
00:19:08,990 --> 00:19:10,860
- three for... - There's no rider.

273
00:19:45,730 --> 00:19:47,660
That's my uncle benjen's horse.

274
00:19:55,240 --> 00:19:56,650
Where's my uncle?

275
00:20:00,710 --> 00:20:01,880
Ned!

276
00:20:04,300 --> 00:20:05,620
It's Robert...

277
00:20:05,930 --> 00:20:08,250
We were hunting... a boar...

278
00:20:15,580 --> 00:20:18,250
I should have spent more time with you,

279
00:20:19,430 --> 00:20:22,050
shown you how to be a man.

280
00:20:25,620 --> 00:20:28,470
I was never meant to be a father.

281
00:20:48,300 --> 00:20:49,650
Go on...

282
00:20:50,290 --> 00:20:52,140
You don't want to see this.

283
00:21:06,820 --> 00:21:08,260
My fault...

284
00:21:08,820 --> 00:21:10,450
Too much wine.

285
00:21:10,920 --> 00:21:12,690
Missed my thrust.

286
00:21:21,880 --> 00:21:23,560
Stinks.

287
00:21:24,500 --> 00:21:26,470
It stinks like death.

288
00:21:27,180 --> 00:21:29,660
Don't think I can't smell it.

289
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:35,760
I paid the bastard back, Ned.

290
00:21:36,220 --> 00:21:38,730
I drove my knife right through his brain.

291
00:21:38,730 --> 00:21:41,090
You ask them if I didn't. Ask them!

292
00:21:42,690 --> 00:21:47,560
I want the funeral feast to be the biggest the kingdoms ever saw.

293
00:21:48,680 --> 00:21:52,490
And I want everyone to taste the boar that got me.

294
00:21:56,030 --> 00:21:59,260
Now leave us, the lot of you I need to talk to Ned.

295
00:22:00,120 --> 00:22:03,030
- Robert, my sweet... - Out! All of you!

296
00:22:22,800 --> 00:22:24,730
You damn fool.

297
00:22:25,250 --> 00:22:27,460
Paper and ink. On the table.

298
00:22:27,510 --> 00:22:29,230
Write down what I say.

299
00:22:37,200 --> 00:22:40,950
In the name of Robert of the House Baratheon

300
00:22:41,370 --> 00:22:46,360
First of... you know how it goes, fill in the damn titles.

301
00:22:47,160 --> 00:22:48,910
I hereby command...

302
00:22:49,100 --> 00:22:53,850
Eddard of House Stark... titles... titles...

303
00:22:54,760 --> 00:22:56,800
to serve as Lord Regent

304
00:22:56,800 --> 00:22:59,960
and Protector of The Realm, upon my death

305
00:23:00,510 --> 00:23:02,710
to rule in my stead

306
00:23:03,500 --> 00:23:06,880
until my son Joffrey comes of age.

307
00:23:24,710 --> 00:23:26,150
Give it over.

308
00:23:41,990 --> 00:23:43,690
Give it to the council

309
00:23:43,780 --> 00:23:45,410
after I'm dead.

310
00:23:46,890 --> 00:23:51,440
At least they'll say I did this right, this one thing.

311
00:23:51,750 --> 00:23:53,690
You'll rule now.

312
00:23:54,640 --> 00:23:56,940
You'll hate it worse than I did...

313
00:23:58,140 --> 00:23:59,900
but you'll do it well.

314
00:24:04,030 --> 00:24:05,500
The girl...

315
00:24:06,360 --> 00:24:08,130
Daenerys...

316
00:24:09,770 --> 00:24:11,240
you were right.

317
00:24:11,240 --> 00:24:15,420
Varys, Littlefinger, my brother, worthless...

318
00:24:16,080 --> 00:24:18,560
No one to tell me "No", but you.

319
00:24:20,440 --> 00:24:21,840
Only you.

320
00:24:25,800 --> 00:24:27,470
Let her live.

321
00:24:29,200 --> 00:24:32,700
- Stop it, if it's not too late. - I will.

322
00:24:33,370 --> 00:24:35,100
And my son...

323
00:24:36,270 --> 00:24:38,190
help him, Ned.

324
00:24:39,250 --> 00:24:41,390
Make him better than me

325
00:24:42,300 --> 00:24:43,830
I'll...

326
00:24:45,260 --> 00:24:48,360
I'll do everything I can to honor your memory.

327
00:24:48,360 --> 00:24:50,470
My memory?

328
00:24:53,190 --> 00:24:55,860
King Robert Baratheon...

329
00:24:56,650 --> 00:24:59,110
murdered by a pig.

330
00:25:02,750 --> 00:25:06,410
Give me something to the pain, and let me die.

331
00:25:20,910 --> 00:25:22,780
Give him milk of the poppy.

332
00:25:30,980 --> 00:25:33,000
He was reeling from the wine.

333
00:25:34,880 --> 00:25:36,670
He commanded us to...

334
00:25:36,730 --> 00:25:38,630
step aside, but...

335
00:25:39,800 --> 00:25:41,420
I failed him.

336
00:25:43,770 --> 00:25:46,650
No man could have protected him from himself.

337
00:25:48,440 --> 00:25:53,440
I wonder, Ser Barristan, who gave the King this wine?

338
00:25:54,460 --> 00:25:57,510
His squire. From the King's own skin.

339
00:25:57,510 --> 00:26:00,700
His squire? The Lannister boy?

340
00:26:00,750 --> 00:26:01,940
Such a dutiful boy to

341
00:26:01,940 --> 00:26:05,310
make sure His Grace did not lack refreshment.

342
00:26:05,930 --> 00:26:09,690
I do hope the poor lad is not blame himself.

343
00:26:17,470 --> 00:26:18,720
His Grace has had a change

344
00:26:18,720 --> 00:26:21,750
of heart concerning Daenerys Targaryen.

345
00:26:23,220 --> 00:26:26,300
Whatever arrangements you made...

346
00:26:26,980 --> 00:26:30,310
unmade them, at once.

347
00:26:30,380 --> 00:26:33,750
I'm afraid those birds have flown.

348
00:26:33,860 --> 00:26:36,510
The girl is likely dead already.

349
00:27:29,950 --> 00:27:30,950
Throne.

350
00:27:33,720 --> 00:27:34,820
Throne.

351
00:28:17,020 --> 00:28:19,250
Can't you help me make him understand?

352
00:28:19,340 --> 00:28:22,090
The Dothraki do things on their own time, for their own reason.

353
00:28:22,100 --> 00:28:25,710
Have patience, Khaleesi. We will go home, I promise you.

354
00:28:25,760 --> 00:28:27,010
My brother...

355
00:28:27,210 --> 00:28:28,130
was a fool, I know,

356
00:28:28,130 --> 00:28:31,210
but he was the rightful heir to the Seven Kingdoms.

357
00:28:32,570 --> 00:28:34,190
Have I said something funny, ser?

358
00:28:34,230 --> 00:28:37,220
Forgive me, khaleesi, but your ancestor, Aegon The Conqueror,

359
00:28:37,220 --> 00:28:39,950
didn't seize six of the kingdoms because it's his right.

360
00:28:39,980 --> 00:28:42,680
He had no right to them, he seized them because he could.

361
00:28:42,790 --> 00:28:44,490
And because he had dragons.

362
00:28:44,790 --> 00:28:47,390
Ah well, having few dragons makes things easier.

363
00:28:48,230 --> 00:28:49,290
You don't believe it?

364
00:28:49,820 --> 00:28:51,590
Have you ever seen a dragon, khaleesi?

365
00:28:52,160 --> 00:28:54,690
I believe what my eyes and ears report.

366
00:28:55,210 --> 00:28:57,550
As for the rest, it was 300 years ago,

367
00:28:57,550 --> 00:28:59,420
who knows what really happened.

368
00:28:59,520 --> 00:29:01,860
Now if you pardon me, I'll seek out the merchant captain,

369
00:29:01,870 --> 00:29:04,870
- See if he has any letters for me. - Well, I'll come with you.

370
00:29:04,880 --> 00:29:06,460
No, no, don't trouble yourself.

371
00:29:06,460 --> 00:29:09,730
Enjoy the market. I'll rejoin you soon enough.

372
00:29:18,610 --> 00:29:20,090
Psst, Jorah the Andal.

373
00:29:22,550 --> 00:29:26,520
The Spider sent his greetings and his congratulations.

374
00:29:29,030 --> 00:29:30,500
A royal pardon--

375
00:29:30,820 --> 00:29:32,180
you can go home now.

376
00:30:12,460 --> 00:30:13,740
My son already has his name,

377
00:30:13,740 --> 00:30:16,850
but I'll try your summerwine. Just a taste.

378
00:30:17,770 --> 00:30:20,030
My lady, you are from Westeros?

379
00:30:20,210 --> 00:30:23,650
You have the honor of addressing Daenerys of the House Targaryen.

380
00:30:23,990 --> 00:30:25,230
Khaleesi of the riding men,

381
00:30:25,230 --> 00:30:27,740
and princess of the Seven Kingdoms.

382
00:30:28,480 --> 00:30:30,610
- Princess. - Rise.

383
00:30:31,090 --> 00:30:32,820
I still like to taste that wine.

384
00:30:33,550 --> 00:30:34,610
That?

385
00:30:35,210 --> 00:30:38,610
Dorne's swill, not worthy of a princess.

386
00:30:38,730 --> 00:30:40,790
I have the dry red from the Arbor.

387
00:30:41,200 --> 00:30:42,760
Nectar of the Gods.

388
00:30:43,180 --> 00:30:44,430
Let me give you a cask.

389
00:30:45,300 --> 00:30:47,770
- A gift! - You honor me, Ser.

390
00:30:47,780 --> 00:30:50,150
The honor... the honor is all mine.

391
00:30:55,490 --> 00:30:57,200
You know there are many in your homeland

392
00:30:57,200 --> 00:30:58,850
that pray for your return, princess.

393
00:30:58,890 --> 00:31:00,850
I hope to repay your kindness someday.

394
00:31:00,850 --> 00:31:01,950
Rakharo.

395
00:31:06,040 --> 00:31:06,910
Is something wrong?

396
00:31:06,910 --> 00:31:09,840
I have a thirst. Open it.

397
00:31:10,860 --> 00:31:13,130
The wine is for the Khaleesi, it's not for the likes of you.

398
00:31:13,180 --> 00:31:14,240
Open it.

399
00:31:26,060 --> 00:31:27,060
Pour.

400
00:31:27,950 --> 00:31:29,730
It would be a crime to drink a wine this rich

401
00:31:29,730 --> 00:31:31,360
without at least giving it time to breathe.

402
00:31:31,360 --> 00:31:32,750
Do as he says.

403
00:31:34,150 --> 00:31:35,850
As the princess command.

404
00:31:48,170 --> 00:31:49,660
Sweet, isn't it?

405
00:31:50,710 --> 00:31:52,470
Can you smell the fruit, Ser?

406
00:31:53,710 --> 00:31:55,210
Taste it, my lord.

407
00:31:55,800 --> 00:31:56,740
Tell me that is not the

408
00:31:56,740 --> 00:31:59,210
finest wine that has ever touch your tongue.

409
00:32:02,840 --> 00:32:04,100
You first.

410
00:32:06,740 --> 00:32:07,850
Me?

411
00:32:08,480 --> 00:32:10,900
I'm afraid I'm not worthy of the vintage.

412
00:32:10,950 --> 00:32:14,000
Beside, is it a poor wine merchant who drink up his own wares.

413
00:32:14,050 --> 00:32:16,540
You will drink.

414
00:32:32,140 --> 00:32:34,540
- Khaleesi! - Stop him!

415
00:32:48,590 --> 00:32:49,630
Come.

416
00:32:56,860 --> 00:32:59,760
You came to us as outlaws.

417
00:33:00,040 --> 00:33:01,460
poachers,

418
00:33:02,070 --> 00:33:03,100
rapers,

419
00:33:03,350 --> 00:33:05,450
killers, thieves.

420
00:33:05,580 --> 00:33:07,020
You came alone,

421
00:33:07,420 --> 00:33:08,900
in chains,

422
00:33:09,400 --> 00:33:12,480
without friends, nor honor.

423
00:33:13,220 --> 00:33:15,010
You came to us rich,

424
00:33:15,490 --> 00:33:17,080
or you came to us poor.

425
00:33:17,570 --> 00:33:21,650
Some of you bear the name of proud houses,

426
00:33:22,200 --> 00:33:25,190
others only bastard names or no names at all.

427
00:33:25,290 --> 00:33:30,290
It does not matter. All that, is in the past.

428
00:33:30,940 --> 00:33:32,030
Here...

429
00:33:33,010 --> 00:33:34,480
on the Wall.

430
00:33:35,310 --> 00:33:37,680
we're all one house.

431
00:33:38,850 --> 00:33:39,990
Tonight...

432
00:33:40,710 --> 00:33:42,280
You're allowed to look happy,

433
00:33:43,360 --> 00:33:45,120
you're going to be a ranger.

434
00:33:46,260 --> 00:33:48,270
Isn't that what you always wanted?

435
00:33:48,950 --> 00:33:50,660
I want to find my uncle.

436
00:33:51,790 --> 00:33:55,090
I know he's alive out there. I know he is.

437
00:33:56,330 --> 00:33:59,510
I wish I could help you, but I'm no ranger.

438
00:34:00,230 --> 00:34:02,340
It's the steward's life for me.

439
00:34:03,190 --> 00:34:05,280
There's honor in being a steward.

440
00:34:06,160 --> 00:34:07,600
Not much, really.

441
00:34:07,980 --> 00:34:09,530
But there's food.

442
00:34:12,370 --> 00:34:13,920
Here,

443
00:34:14,880 --> 00:34:16,930
you begin anew.

444
00:34:23,880 --> 00:34:27,570
A man of the Night's Watch,

445
00:34:29,020 --> 00:34:31,710
lives his life for the realm.

446
00:34:33,350 --> 00:34:34,960
Not for a king,

447
00:34:35,390 --> 00:34:36,570
or a Lord,

448
00:34:36,760 --> 00:34:40,420
or the honor of this house or that house.

449
00:34:40,910 --> 00:34:43,470
Not for gold nor glory

450
00:34:43,600 --> 00:34:45,430
or women's love.

451
00:34:46,350 --> 00:34:47,750
But for the realm

452
00:34:48,190 --> 00:34:50,430
and all the people in it.

453
00:34:51,260 --> 00:34:55,000
You've all learned the words of the vow.

454
00:34:55,100 --> 00:34:58,030
Think carefully before you say them.

455
00:34:58,690 --> 00:35:00,810
The penalty for desertion

456
00:35:01,580 --> 00:35:02,940
is death.

457
00:35:08,610 --> 00:35:10,590
You can take your vows here...

458
00:35:10,820 --> 00:35:12,020
tonight...

459
00:35:12,600 --> 00:35:13,690
at sunset.

460
00:35:15,000 --> 00:35:17,560
Do any of you still keep the Old Gods?

461
00:35:19,630 --> 00:35:21,140
I do, my lord.

462
00:35:21,540 --> 00:35:22,720
Do you want to take your vows

463
00:35:22,720 --> 00:35:24,980
before the heart tree, as your uncle did?

464
00:35:25,050 --> 00:35:26,110
Yes, my lord.

465
00:35:26,220 --> 00:35:29,170
You'll find the weirwoods, a mile north of the Wall

466
00:35:29,260 --> 00:35:31,320
and your Old Gods too, maybe.

467
00:35:33,070 --> 00:35:34,200
My Lord?

468
00:35:35,070 --> 00:35:36,290
Might I go as well?

469
00:35:36,310 --> 00:35:38,600
Is House Tarly keep the Old Gods?

470
00:35:38,830 --> 00:35:40,240
No, my lord.

471
00:35:40,980 --> 00:35:43,200
I was name in the light of the Seven,

472
00:35:43,300 --> 00:35:46,000
as my father was and his father before him.

473
00:35:46,110 --> 00:35:48,340
Why would you forsake,

474
00:35:48,350 --> 00:35:49,740
the Gods of your father and your house?

475
00:35:52,160 --> 00:35:54,790
The Night's Watch is my house now.

476
00:35:54,790 --> 00:35:57,470
The Seven have never answer my prayers,

477
00:35:57,920 --> 00:35:59,960
perhaps the Old Gods will.

478
00:36:01,490 --> 00:36:02,740
As you wish, lad.

479
00:36:04,110 --> 00:36:06,950
You all been assigned an order,

480
00:36:07,220 --> 00:36:09,540
according to our needs,

481
00:36:10,140 --> 00:36:12,240
and your strength.

482
00:36:12,310 --> 00:36:14,500
Halder to the builders.

483
00:36:15,490 --> 00:36:17,190
Pyp to the stewards.

484
00:36:17,330 --> 00:36:18,650
Tod to the builders.

485
00:36:18,950 --> 00:36:20,300
Grenn to the rangers.

486
00:36:20,390 --> 00:36:21,900
Samwell to the stewards.

487
00:36:22,610 --> 00:36:24,150
Matthar to the rangers.

488
00:36:24,150 --> 00:36:25,550
Dareon to the stewards.

489
00:36:26,060 --> 00:36:27,840
Balian to the rangers.

490
00:36:28,160 --> 00:36:29,720
Rast to the rangers.

491
00:36:29,900 --> 00:36:31,570
Jon to the stewards.

492
00:36:31,780 --> 00:36:33,120
Rancer to the builders.

493
00:36:33,410 --> 00:36:36,290
Echiel to the builders. Gordo to the stewards.

494
00:36:36,420 --> 00:36:39,590
Niko to the rangers. Escan to the rangers.

495
00:36:39,900 --> 00:36:42,780
Vorkoy to the builders. Joby to the stables.

496
00:36:43,070 --> 00:36:44,390
Mink to the kitchens.

497
00:36:44,610 --> 00:36:46,170
Allo to the builders.

498
00:36:46,320 --> 00:36:48,650
Nelugo to the rangers.

499
00:36:48,910 --> 00:36:51,780
May all the Gods preserve you.

500
00:36:57,360 --> 00:36:59,540
Rangers, with me.

501
00:37:00,470 --> 00:37:01,610
Builders!

502
00:37:21,220 --> 00:37:22,310
Samwell,

503
00:37:22,640 --> 00:37:25,640
you will assisst me in the rookery and the library.

504
00:37:25,890 --> 00:37:26,890
Pyp,

505
00:37:27,030 --> 00:37:29,960
you will report to Bowen Marsh, in the kitchens.

506
00:37:30,090 --> 00:37:34,130
Luke, report to one-eyed Joe in the stables.

507
00:37:34,860 --> 00:37:38,550
Dareon, we are sending you to Eastwatch.

508
00:37:38,720 --> 00:37:41,440
present yourself to Borcas when you arrive.

509
00:37:41,600 --> 00:37:44,950
Make no comment about his nose.

510
00:37:46,480 --> 00:37:47,510
Jon Snow,

511
00:37:47,730 --> 00:37:49,150
Lord Commander Mormont

512
00:37:49,150 --> 00:37:51,930
has requested you for his personal steward.

513
00:37:53,570 --> 00:37:55,050
Will I serve the Lord Commander's meal,

514
00:37:55,050 --> 00:37:57,040
and fetch hot water for his bath?

515
00:37:57,070 --> 00:37:58,070
Certainly.

516
00:37:58,270 --> 00:38:00,770
And keep a fire burning in his chambers,

517
00:38:00,770 --> 00:38:03,570
change his sheets and blankets daily

518
00:38:03,650 --> 00:38:07,460
and do everything else the Lord Commander requires of you.

519
00:38:10,490 --> 00:38:12,020
Do you take me for a servant?

520
00:38:12,120 --> 00:38:15,040
We took you for a man of the Night's Watch.

521
00:38:15,140 --> 00:38:17,980
But perhaps we were wrong in that.

522
00:38:18,640 --> 00:38:19,910
May I go?

523
00:38:20,260 --> 00:38:21,610
As you wish.

524
00:38:27,340 --> 00:38:29,650
Jon, Wait!

525
00:38:29,770 --> 00:38:31,470
Don't you see what they're doing?

526
00:38:31,470 --> 00:38:33,350
I see Ser Alliser's revenge, that's all.

527
00:38:33,360 --> 00:38:35,150
he wanted it and he got it.

528
00:38:35,190 --> 00:38:37,420
Stewards are nothing but maids!

529
00:38:37,420 --> 00:38:40,090
I'm a better swordsman and rider than any of you!

530
00:38:40,190 --> 00:38:41,550
It's not fair!

531
00:38:41,630 --> 00:38:43,200
Fair?

532
00:38:43,710 --> 00:38:45,810
I was singing for a high lord at Acorn Hall

533
00:38:45,810 --> 00:38:47,580
when he put his hand in my leg

534
00:38:47,580 --> 00:38:48,720
and he wanted to see my cock.

535
00:38:48,800 --> 00:38:50,290
I pushed him away and he said

536
00:38:50,330 --> 00:38:52,830
he'd have my hands cut off for stealing their silver.

537
00:38:52,840 --> 00:38:54,770
So now I'm here, at the end of the world

538
00:38:54,780 --> 00:38:57,720
where no one to sing for but old men and little shits like you.

539
00:38:57,730 --> 00:38:59,650
I'll never see my family again.

540
00:38:59,650 --> 00:39:01,530
I'll never be inside a woman again.

541
00:39:01,530 --> 00:39:03,100
So don't tell me about fair.

542
00:39:03,100 --> 00:39:05,120
I thought you were caught stealing a wheel of cheese

543
00:39:05,120 --> 00:39:07,010
for your starving sister?

544
00:39:07,050 --> 00:39:08,100
You think I was gonna tell a bunch of strangers

545
00:39:08,100 --> 00:39:11,300
that a high lord tried to grab my cock?

546
00:39:13,650 --> 00:39:15,640
Could you sing me a song, Pyp?

547
00:39:15,890 --> 00:39:17,960
I'd like to hear a song.

548
00:39:22,480 --> 00:39:23,760
Now listen to me,

549
00:39:24,220 --> 00:39:27,520
the old man is the Lord Commander of The Night's Watch.

550
00:39:27,570 --> 00:39:29,990
You will be with him day and night,

551
00:39:29,990 --> 00:39:32,210
yes, you will clean his clothes.

552
00:39:32,210 --> 00:39:34,570
But you will also take his letters,

553
00:39:34,570 --> 00:39:37,840
attend him at meeting, squire for him in battle.

554
00:39:38,030 --> 00:39:41,400
You'll know everything, be part of everything.

555
00:39:41,600 --> 00:39:44,050
And he asked for you himself.

556
00:39:44,710 --> 00:39:47,610
He wants to groom you for command.

557
00:39:52,790 --> 00:39:53,890
I just...

558
00:39:55,210 --> 00:39:57,410
I always wanted to be a ranger.

559
00:39:59,620 --> 00:40:01,670
I always wanted to be a wizard.

560
00:40:04,990 --> 00:40:06,280
What?

561
00:40:06,640 --> 00:40:08,150
No, I'm serious.

562
00:40:08,150 --> 00:40:10,960
So you'll stay and say your words with me?

563
00:40:17,410 --> 00:40:18,760
Lord Stark,

564
00:40:19,310 --> 00:40:20,650
a moment?

565
00:40:21,800 --> 00:40:23,440
Alone if you will.

566
00:40:33,300 --> 00:40:35,440
He named you Protector of The Realm.

567
00:40:37,080 --> 00:40:38,260
He did.

568
00:40:38,780 --> 00:40:40,240
She won't care.

569
00:40:40,320 --> 00:40:43,280
Give me an hour and I can put a hundred of swords at your command.

570
00:40:44,050 --> 00:40:47,310
- And what should I do with a hundred swords? - Strike!

571
00:40:47,310 --> 00:40:49,290
Tonight while the castle sleeps.

572
00:40:49,690 --> 00:40:52,840
We must get Joffrey away from his mother and into our custody.

573
00:40:53,040 --> 00:40:54,460
Protector of The Realm or no,

574
00:40:54,460 --> 00:40:56,850
he who holds the king holds the kingdom.

575
00:40:57,920 --> 00:41:00,890
Every moment you delay gives Cersei another moment to prepare.

576
00:41:01,110 --> 00:41:04,170
By the time Robert dies, it will be too late for the both of us.

577
00:41:04,170 --> 00:41:05,750
What about Stannis?

578
00:41:05,990 --> 00:41:07,890
Saving the Seven Kingdoms from Cersei

579
00:41:07,890 --> 00:41:09,810
and delivering them to Stannis?

580
00:41:09,940 --> 00:41:12,200
You have odd notion about "protecting the realm".

581
00:41:12,200 --> 00:41:13,940
Stannis is your older brother.

582
00:41:13,940 --> 00:41:16,330
This isn't about the bloody line of succession.

583
00:41:16,870 --> 00:41:18,830
That didn't matter when you rebelled against the Mad King

584
00:41:18,830 --> 00:41:20,610
it shouldn't matter now.

585
00:41:22,260 --> 00:41:24,130
What's best for the kingdoms?

586
00:41:24,890 --> 00:41:27,350
What's best for the people we rule?

587
00:41:28,740 --> 00:41:30,910
We all know what Stannis is.

588
00:41:31,700 --> 00:41:34,480
He inspires no love or loyalty.

589
00:41:34,740 --> 00:41:36,270
He's not a king.

590
00:41:37,680 --> 00:41:39,200
I am.

591
00:41:45,930 --> 00:41:47,930
Stannis is a commander.

592
00:41:48,690 --> 00:41:50,850
He's led men into war twice.

593
00:41:51,060 --> 00:41:52,620
He destroyed the Greyjoy fleet...

594
00:41:52,620 --> 00:41:54,500
Yes, he's a good soldier, everyone knows that.

595
00:41:54,500 --> 00:41:55,940
So was Robert.

596
00:41:56,980 --> 00:41:59,000
Tell me something: Do you still believe

597
00:41:59,000 --> 00:42:00,970
good soldiers make good kings?

598
00:42:06,490 --> 00:42:08,330
I will not dishonor Robert's last hours

599
00:42:08,330 --> 00:42:10,450
by shedding blood in his halls

600
00:42:11,240 --> 00:42:13,930
and dragging frightened children from their beds.

601
00:42:27,260 --> 00:42:29,770
You will sail to Dragonstone tonight.

602
00:42:30,180 --> 00:42:32,770
You will place this in the hand of Stannis Baratheon.

603
00:42:34,380 --> 00:42:35,830
Not his steward.

604
00:42:37,150 --> 00:42:39,250
Not his captain of the guard.

605
00:42:39,620 --> 00:42:41,350
And not his wife.

606
00:42:47,310 --> 00:42:49,140
Only Stannis himself.

607
00:42:50,310 --> 00:42:52,030
Yes, my lord.

608
00:42:53,960 --> 00:42:55,510
Now leave us.

609
00:43:04,920 --> 00:43:07,080
My lord protector.

610
00:43:12,790 --> 00:43:15,320
The king has no trueborn sons.

611
00:43:15,710 --> 00:43:19,680
Joffrey and Tommen are Jaime Lannister's bastards.

612
00:43:20,560 --> 00:43:22,800
So when the king dies...

613
00:43:22,800 --> 00:43:25,180
The throne passes to his brother

614
00:43:26,340 --> 00:43:27,840
Lord Stannis.

615
00:43:28,900 --> 00:43:30,410
So it would seem.

616
00:43:31,720 --> 00:43:34,350
- Unless... - There is no "unless"!

617
00:43:34,430 --> 00:43:36,730
He is the rightful heir. Nothing can change that.

618
00:43:36,760 --> 00:43:38,990
And he cannot take the throne without your help.

619
00:43:38,990 --> 00:43:40,550
You would be wise to deny it to him

620
00:43:40,550 --> 00:43:43,140
and to make sure Joffrey succeeds.

621
00:43:46,240 --> 00:43:48,260
Do you have a shred of honor?

622
00:43:48,700 --> 00:43:52,450
You're now Hand of The King and Protector of The Realm,

623
00:43:52,450 --> 00:43:55,030
all the power is yours, you need only...

624
00:43:55,280 --> 00:43:58,050
reach out and take it.

625
00:43:58,050 --> 00:44:01,250
Make peace with the Lannisters. Release The Imp.

626
00:44:01,490 --> 00:44:03,690
Wed your daughter to Joffrey.

627
00:44:04,140 --> 00:44:05,970
We have plenty of time to get rid of Stannis

628
00:44:05,970 --> 00:44:07,190
and if Joffrey seems likely

629
00:44:07,190 --> 00:44:09,600
to cause problems when he comes into his throne,

630
00:44:09,600 --> 00:44:11,990
we simply reveal his little secret

631
00:44:11,990 --> 00:44:15,200
- and seat Lord Renly there instead. - We?

632
00:44:15,200 --> 00:44:18,230
You'll need someone to share these burdens, I assure you,

633
00:44:19,160 --> 00:44:21,670
my price would be modest.

634
00:44:22,220 --> 00:44:24,580
What you suggest is treason.

635
00:44:25,200 --> 00:44:27,140
Only if we lose.

636
00:44:29,270 --> 00:44:31,860
Make peace with the Lannisters, you say...

637
00:44:33,630 --> 00:44:35,650
with the people who tried to murder my boy.

638
00:44:35,680 --> 00:44:38,600
We only make peace with our enemies, my lord.

639
00:44:38,990 --> 00:44:41,440
That's why it's called "Making peace".

640
00:44:41,830 --> 00:44:43,190
No.

641
00:44:44,010 --> 00:44:45,460
I won't do it.

642
00:44:45,650 --> 00:44:49,500
- So it will be Stannis and war? - There is no other choice.

643
00:44:50,660 --> 00:44:52,160
He is the heir.

644
00:44:53,110 --> 00:44:56,950
So why did you call me here? Not for my wisdom, clearly.

645
00:44:58,430 --> 00:45:00,770
You promised Catelyn you would help me.

646
00:45:00,770 --> 00:45:03,890
The queen has a dozen knights and hundred man-at-arms.

647
00:45:03,890 --> 00:45:07,060
Enough to overwhelm what remains of my household guard.

648
00:45:07,620 --> 00:45:09,510
I need the Gold Cloaks.

649
00:45:10,470 --> 00:45:12,860
The City Watch is 2,000 strong,

650
00:45:13,500 --> 00:45:15,870
and sworn to defend the king's peace.

651
00:45:18,850 --> 00:45:20,220
Look at you.

652
00:45:21,350 --> 00:45:25,460
You know what you want me to do, you know it has to be done.

653
00:45:25,730 --> 00:45:28,030
But it's not honorable so

654
00:45:28,520 --> 00:45:30,740
the words stick in your throat.

655
00:45:31,340 --> 00:45:33,740
When the Queen proclaims one king

656
00:45:33,740 --> 00:45:35,580
and the Hand proclaim another,

657
00:45:35,580 --> 00:45:38,570
whose peace to the Gold Cloaks protect?

658
00:45:39,880 --> 00:45:41,750
Who do they follow?

659
00:45:46,680 --> 00:45:48,620
The man who pays them.

660
00:46:34,110 --> 00:46:38,340
Hear my words and bear witness to my vow.

661
00:46:38,730 --> 00:46:41,860
Night gathers and now my watch begins.

662
00:46:42,060 --> 00:46:44,910
It shall not end until my death.

663
00:46:45,270 --> 00:46:50,270
I shall take no wife, hold no lands, father no children.

664
00:46:51,270 --> 00:46:54,900
I shall wear no crowns and win no glory.

665
00:46:55,170 --> 00:46:58,520
I shall live and die at my post.

666
00:46:58,780 --> 00:47:01,710
I am the sword in the darkness.

667
00:47:01,790 --> 00:47:04,600
I am the watcher on the walls.

668
00:47:04,600 --> 00:47:08,440
I am the shield that guards the realm of men.

669
00:47:08,570 --> 00:47:12,870
I pledge my life and honor to the Night's Watch,

670
00:47:12,870 --> 00:47:16,250
for this night and all the nights to come.

671
00:47:16,530 --> 00:47:18,230
You knelt as boys.

672
00:47:18,730 --> 00:47:21,540
Rise now as men of the Night's Watch.

673
00:47:34,750 --> 00:47:36,840
- Well done. - Well done.

674
00:47:44,110 --> 00:47:45,120
What's he got there?

675
00:47:45,750 --> 00:47:47,120
To me, Ghost.

676
00:47:47,120 --> 00:47:48,370
Bring it here.

677
00:47:50,380 --> 00:47:52,050
Gods be good!

678
00:47:59,310 --> 00:48:00,830
What will they do to him?

679
00:48:04,540 --> 00:48:05,720
When the khalasar rides,

680
00:48:05,760 --> 00:48:06,980
he'll be leashed to a saddle and

681
00:48:06,980 --> 00:48:10,230
forced to run behind the horses for as long as he can.

682
00:48:10,620 --> 00:48:12,040
And when he falls?

683
00:48:13,870 --> 00:48:16,590
I saw a man last nine miles once.

684
00:48:18,350 --> 00:48:20,420
King Robert still wants me dead.

685
00:48:20,420 --> 00:48:23,170
This poisoner was the first. He won't be the last.

686
00:48:23,460 --> 00:48:26,800
I thought he'd leave me alone, now that my brother is gone.

687
00:48:26,800 --> 00:48:29,190
He will never leave you alone.

688
00:48:30,000 --> 00:48:33,170
If you ride to darkest Asshai, his assassins will follow you.

689
00:48:33,170 --> 00:48:35,680
If you sail all the way to the Basilisk Isles,

690
00:48:35,680 --> 00:48:37,000
his spy would tell him.

691
00:48:37,000 --> 00:48:39,810
He will never abandon the hunt.

692
00:48:40,490 --> 00:48:42,370
You are a Targaryen.

693
00:48:42,460 --> 00:48:44,240
The last Targaryen.

694
00:48:44,240 --> 00:48:46,160
Your son will have Targaryen blood

695
00:48:46,160 --> 00:48:48,870
with 40,000 riders behind him.

696
00:48:50,580 --> 00:48:52,380
He will not have my son.

697
00:48:53,470 --> 00:48:55,680
He will not have you either, Khaleesi.

698
00:51:58,300 --> 00:51:59,670
Lord Stark!

699
00:52:00,230 --> 00:52:02,150
- Stop! - No, all right.

700
00:52:02,480 --> 00:52:04,870
- It's all right. Let him through. - Lord Stark,

701
00:52:04,910 --> 00:52:05,820
King Joffrey and the Queen Regent

702
00:52:05,820 --> 00:52:07,680
request you presence in the throne room.

703
00:52:07,680 --> 00:52:09,120
King Joffrey?

704
00:52:09,500 --> 00:52:12,510
King Robert is gone. The Gods give him rest.

705
00:52:25,050 --> 00:52:27,540
All is accomplished. The City Watch is yours.

706
00:52:27,550 --> 00:52:28,900
Good.

707
00:52:29,800 --> 00:52:31,780
Is Lord Renly joining us?

708
00:52:33,440 --> 00:52:36,990
I fear Lord Renly has left the city.

709
00:52:37,320 --> 00:52:40,480
He rode through the Old Gate an hour before dawn

710
00:52:40,480 --> 00:52:44,640
with ser Loras Tyrell and some 50 retainers.

711
00:52:44,650 --> 00:52:48,690
Last seen galloping south in some haste.

712
00:53:09,040 --> 00:53:11,000
We stand behind you, lord Stark.

713
00:53:20,460 --> 00:53:25,200
All hail His Grace, Joffrey of Houses Baratheon and Lannister,

714
00:53:25,200 --> 00:53:26,670
the First of His Name,

715
00:53:26,980 --> 00:53:29,200
King of The Andals, and The First Men,

716
00:53:29,350 --> 00:53:34,350
Lord of The Seven Kingdoms and Protector of The Realm.

717
00:53:52,380 --> 00:53:53,760
I command the council to make

718
00:53:53,760 --> 00:53:56,640
all necessary arrangements for my coronation.

719
00:53:56,640 --> 00:53:59,120
I wish to be crowned within the fortnight.

720
00:53:59,480 --> 00:54:04,110
Today I shall accept oaths of fealty from my loyal councilors.

721
00:54:08,340 --> 00:54:09,760
Ser Barristan,

722
00:54:10,130 --> 00:54:13,060
I believe no men here could ever question your honor.

723
00:54:24,590 --> 00:54:26,210
King Robert seal.

724
00:54:26,630 --> 00:54:27,960
Unbroken.

725
00:54:35,380 --> 00:54:38,340
Lord Eddard Stark is herein named

726
00:54:38,910 --> 00:54:40,920
Protector of The Realm,

727
00:54:41,770 --> 00:54:43,870
to rule as regent

728
00:54:43,870 --> 00:54:46,410
until the heir come of age.

729
00:54:47,490 --> 00:54:49,860
May I see that letter, ser Barristan?

730
00:54:58,750 --> 00:55:00,540
Protector of The Realm.

731
00:55:04,520 --> 00:55:06,950
Is this meant to be your shield, Lord Stark?

732
00:55:08,060 --> 00:55:09,730
A piece of paper?

733
00:55:13,190 --> 00:55:14,690
Those were the king's words.

734
00:55:14,690 --> 00:55:16,630
We have a new king now.

735
00:55:19,010 --> 00:55:22,940
Lord Eddard, when we last spoke you offered me some counsel.

736
00:55:23,080 --> 00:55:25,220
Allow me to return the courtesy.

737
00:55:25,740 --> 00:55:27,470
Bend the knee, my lord.

738
00:55:27,810 --> 00:55:31,170
Bend the knee and swear loyalty to my son.

739
00:55:31,790 --> 00:55:34,820
And we shall allow you to live out your days in the grey waste

740
00:55:34,820 --> 00:55:36,550
you call home.

741
00:55:36,980 --> 00:55:39,260
Your son has no claim to the throne.

742
00:55:39,640 --> 00:55:40,490
Liar!

743
00:55:40,500 --> 00:55:43,200
You condemn yourself with your own mouth, lord Stark.

744
00:55:43,630 --> 00:55:45,940
Ser Barristan, seize this traitor.

745
00:55:46,720 --> 00:55:49,450
Ser Barristan is a good man, a loyal man. Do him no harm.

746
00:55:52,990 --> 00:55:54,480
You think you stands alone?

747
00:55:57,440 --> 00:56:00,550
Kill him! Kill all of them! I command it!

748
00:56:00,860 --> 00:56:02,080
Commander!

749
00:56:02,670 --> 00:56:05,090
Take the queen and her children into custody.

750
00:56:05,360 --> 00:56:06,940
Escort them back to the royal apartments

751
00:56:06,950 --> 00:56:09,250
and keep them there, under guard.

752
00:56:09,250 --> 00:56:10,690
Men of the watch!

753
00:56:14,990 --> 00:56:16,800
I want no bloodshed.

754
00:56:17,560 --> 00:56:21,770
Tell your men to lay down their swords. No one needs to die.

755
00:56:23,940 --> 00:56:25,430
Now!

756
00:56:36,750 --> 00:56:39,340
I did warn you not to trust me.

